+/* Echoes pen input on a transparent canvas above the video while the real ink
+ * makes the round trip through the server.
+ *
+ * Both halves of Xournal++'s pen pipeline are reproduced here: which points
+ * reach the stroke (the arithmetic stabilizer, the 0.3-document-unit admission
+ * threshold, the width subdivision and the pen-up spline tail) and how they are
+ * rasterised (the union of one capsule per segment, filled once). Everything
+ * runs in document units; only the final transform maps them to the screen.
+ *
+ * A stroke is echoed whole until the video has caught up with its last point.
+ * The frames decide when that is, rather than a fixed window into the past:
+ * every frame carries the instant it was captured, so the echo is retired only
+ * once a frame captured after the server could have drawn the stroke has
+ * actually been painted. When the video stalls the cutoff stalls with it and
+ * the echo stays up, which is the behaviour a fixed window cannot have: it
+ * retires ink on schedule whether or not the video arrived, and the missing ink
+ * shows as a gap behind the pen.
+ *
+ * Echoing a stroke whole means drawing over the part of it the video has
+ * already delivered. Two things keep that from reading as doubled ink, and both
+ * are needed:
+ *
+ *   - The echo is rasterised on the capture's pixel grid and left for the
+ *     browser to stretch into the video box, so it goes through the same
+ *     resampling the video does. Rasterised at the display's own resolution it
+ *     is a crisp line lying on a resampled one, and the two together read as
+ *     bolder than either.
+ *   - The canvas is blended with `darken`, over a backdrop painted in the
+ *     blend's identity colour (white for `darken`, black for `lighten`). That
+ *     turns the echo's antialiasing from an alpha, which composites over the
+ *     video's copy and adds to it, into a colour, and the blend keeps whichever
+ *     of the two is darker. Ink drawn over ink already on the video then
+ *     changes nothing.
+ *
+ * Overdraw being free is also what lets the capsule union be built once and
+ * appended to as the stroke grows; skipping a prefix would need it rebuilt.
+ *
+ * The echo is dropped outright at pen-up rather than fading: Xournal++'s shape
+ * recognizer can replace the finished stroke with something else entirely, so
+ * nothing about it can be trusted past the handoff. */
